What type of carbonyl compound is primarily produced when Grignard reagents react with carbon dioxide (CO₂)?
</USER_REQUEST>

<GROUND_TRUTH>
When Grignard reagents react with carbon dioxide (CO₂), they primarily produce carboxylic acids. The reaction proceeds as follows:
\[ \text{R-Mg-X} + \text{CO}_2 \rightarrow \text{R-COOH} + \text{Mg(OH)X} \]
