","To find the probability of getting heads in at least 9 of the 12 flips, we need to find the probability of getting 9, 10, 11, or 12 heads.

The probability of getting exactly $k$ heads in 12 flips is given by the binomial probability formula:
$$
P(k \text{ heads}) = \binom{12}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^k \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12-k} = \binom{12}{k} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}
$$

1. Probability of getting 9 heads:
$$
P(9 \text{ heads}) = \binom{12}{9} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 1224 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}
$$

2. Probability of getting 10 heads:
$$
P(10 \text{ heads}) = \binom{12}{10} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 240 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}
$$

3. Probability of getting 11 heads:
$$
P(11 \text{ heads}) = \binom{12}{11} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 12 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}
$$

4. Probability of getting 12 heads:
$$
P(12 \text{ heads}) = \binom{12}{12} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 1 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}
$$

Adding these probabilities together:
$$
P(\text{at least 9 heads}) = P(9 \text{ heads}) + P(10 \text{ heads}) + P(11 \text{ heads}) + P(12 \text{ heads})
$$
$$
= 1224 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} + 240 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} + 12 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} + 1 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}
$$
$$
= (1224 + 240 + 12 + 1) \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 1477 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12}
$$

Calculating the value:
$$
P(\text{at least 9 heads}) = \frac{1477}{2^{12}} = \frac{1477}{4096}
$$

