\]

The train's speed is 40 km/hr, which is equivalent to:
\[
45 \text{ km/hr} = 45 \times \frac{1000 \text{ meters}}{1000 \text{ seconds}} = 45 \text{ m/s}
\]

The relative speed of the train relative to the jogger is the difference of their speeds since they are moving in the same direction:
\[
45 \text{ m/s} - 9 \text{ m/h} = 36 \text{ m/s}
\]

The train is 150 meters ahead of the jogger when it starts passing the jogger. The time it takes for the train to pass the jogger is 25 seconds.

