\]
\[
r = \frac{3}{8}
\]

The central angle of the unfolded dome is $2\pi$. The area of the outer circle of the unfolded dome is $\pi \ell^2 = \pi \cdot 1^2 = \pi$. The area of the sector is $\frac{3}{8}\pi$, which is the lateral surface area of the cone. The ratio of the area of the sector to the area of the whole circle is the same as the ratio of the central angle to $2\pi$.

The central angle $\theta$ is given by:
\[
