3. **Construct a Continuous \( f \):**  
   Define a characteristic function \( \chi_C \) on \( \mathcal{F} \):  
   \[
   \chi_C(A) = 1 \quad \text{if } A \subset C, \quad \text{and} \quad \0 \quad \text{if } A \notin C.
   \]  
   Since \( C \) is countable, \( \chi_C \) is measurable.  
   Now, define a continuous function \( f \) on \( \mathcal{F} \) as:  
   \[
   f(x) = \chi_C(x) \quad \text{for all } x \in \mathcal{F}.
