\[
\text{Time on Earth} = \frac{\text{Time on the ship}}{\sqrt{1 - \frac{v^2}{v^2^2}}}
\]

Substituting the given values:

\[
\text{Time on Earth} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{1 - \frac{0.6^2}{1}}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{1 - 0.36}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{0.64}} = \frac{3}{0.8} = 3.75 \text{ seconds}
