</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To solve this problem, we need to consider the concept of time delay. The time delay is the time on the moving system (in this case, the ship) is 3 seconds.

To find the time on the clock in the carerer, we can use the time dilation formula:

\[
\text{Time on Earth} = \frac{\text{Time on the ship}}{\sqrt{1 - \frac{v^2}{v^2^2}}}
\]

Substituting the given values:

\[
\text{Time on Earth} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{1 - \frac{0.6^2}{1}}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{1 - 0.36}} = \frac{3}{\sqrt{0.64}} = \frac{3}{0.8} = 3.75 \text{ seconds}
\]

Thus, the time on the coiler is 3.75 seconds.
